WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.260
In 1779, David Hume gave one of his
characters some very old questions.

2
00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:09.540
Is God willing to prevent
evil, but not able?

3
00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:11.630
Then God is not all-powerful.

4
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:13.930
Is God able, but not willing?

5
00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.770
Then God is not good.

6
00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:18.230
So where does evil come from?

7
00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:21.290
Now picture a fawn,
trapped in a forest fire,

8
00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:24.220
suffering for days, unseen.

9
00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:28.670
If God is all-powerful and
all-loving, why is there malaria?

10
00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.580
Is that a proof, or just a problem?

11
00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:33.190
In this mission, you'll build J.

12
00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:33.350
L.

13
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.910
Mackie's inconsistent triad, step by step.

14
00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:41.470
Then you'll meet William Rowe, and
ask what this unseen suffering shows.

15
00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:46.840
Your mission: find out whether evil
disproves God or only makes belief harder.
